_STYLE_BIBLE = """
STYLE BIBLE: official "Grand Theft Auto VI" key-art / loading-screen illustration.

MEDIUM (most important)
- A high-end, modern digital painting with vector-sharp shape edges AND rich, luminous, smooth-blended volume inside the shapes: the polished, glossy, high-resolution look of AAA game promotional art (like a premium stylized digital illustration with cinematic lighting).
- Every form has real 3D volume: light wraps around faces, arms, hair, fabric and metal with smooth gradients inside crisp-edged shadow and light shapes. It is NOT flat, NOT a retro/vintage comic, NOT a print with paper grain.
- It is NOT a photograph, NOT a 3D/CGI render, NOT anime or manga, NOT a children's cartoon, NOT a generic synthwave/vaporwave vector.
- Finish: clean, ultra-sharp, high-definition and glossy. ABSOLUTELY no paper texture, no film grain, no noise, no halftone dots, no screen-print or newspaper effect, no faded/matte retro look.

FACES AND ANATOMY
- Realistic adult proportions (about 7.5 heads tall), natural leg length, real muscle and bone structure. Never elongated legs, never exaggerated pin-up curves, never doll faces.
- Faces are realistic and individual: normal-sized eyes with heavy upper lids, defined thick eyebrows, strong nose and jaw, full lips, visible pores/stubble, slight scowl or cool, serious, defiant stare. No big shiny anime eyes, no sweet smiles unless the user asks.
- Faces are sculpted with a sharp-edged shadow shape (under the brow, along the nose, under the cheekbone, under the lip, along the jaw and neck) whose interior is a smooth warm-to-violet gradient, plus a soft light-wrap on the lit edge. Faces must have clear 3D volume: one side of the face in warm light, the other side falling into rich magenta/violet shadow with reflected pink light. Detailed, finished, realistic faces with defined eyelids, tear ducts, lashes, lip highlights, nostrils and ears.
- Beard stubble is fine stipple/short strokes with soft shading; hair is richly rendered: large clumped locks with many layered glossy highlights, bright rim-lit edges, violet/burgundy/magenta reflections and deep inner shadows, individual strand lines flowing along the lock; curly hair has defined ringlets, each with its own highlight and shadow.
- Muscles, collarbones, veins, tendons and knuckles are modeled with sharp-edged shadow shapes plus smooth gradient transitions inside. Skin is sun-tanned and GLOSSY, with a satiny specular sheen on forehead, nose, cheekbones, shoulders, collarbones, biceps, knees and shins, and a thin sweat sheen on the lit side.

LINEWORK
- Thin, delicate, precise contour in a darker shade of each object's own color (deep burgundy on skin, dark indigo on denim, dark green on cargo), never thick, never uniform black, never a cartoon sticker outline. Tapered: slightly heavier on the shadow side, fading to almost nothing or disappearing completely on the rim-lit side so the light glows over the edge.
- Additional hairline interior lines for clothing folds, hair strands, jewelry, tattoos, stitching and metal edges.

SHADING AND LIGHT
- CINEMATIC SIDE/BACK LIGHTING (critical): one dominant low golden-orange sun placed behind and to the side of the characters, so the light rakes across them. About 40 to 50 percent of each face and body is in shadow; never light a subject evenly from the front and never flat-light the scene.
- LUMINOUS RIM LIGHT: a bright, glowing, cream/yellow-white rim light along the edge of hair, cheek, nose, lips, shoulders, arms, fingers and clothing on the sun side, with a soft bloom/glow bleeding slightly over the edge, plus warm sun-glints and a subtle lens-glow near the sun.
- Skin gradient: warm orange-gold on the lit side, soft terracotta/rose at the terminator, deep magenta and violet in the shadow, hot-pink reflected bounce light inside the shadow, and a subtle cool blue-teal fill on the far edge from the sky. Add subtle subsurface warmth (red-orange glow) where light passes through ears, nostrils, lips and fingers.
- Specular highlights: crisp cream-white glints with soft falloff on cheekbone, nose bridge, brow, lower lip, forehead, shoulders, arms, hair locks, gold chains, jewelry, watches, glass, bottles, car paint and chrome. Glossy materials (glass, metal, car body, wet skin) have strong reflections of the sunset.
- Ambient occlusion and contact shadows: soft darker violet shading where objects meet (under chin, under hair, under collars, folds of clothing, under arms, where hands touch surfaces) for depth and weight.
- Clothing and objects follow the same lighting: smooth-gradient volume with sharp-edged shadow shapes tinted violet/blue/magenta and warm highlights, visible fabric sheen on satin/synthetic cloth, fold highlights; shadows are NEVER neutral gray or black and NEVER flat fill.
- Strong warm vs cool contrast and a high-contrast, high-dynamic-range glow between the lit and shadow sides is the heart of the look; the image should feel luminous and glossy, like sunlight on skin.

COLOR PALETTE (use these as the dominant colors)
- Sky gradient: deep violet #5B3FA0 -> purple #8A5CC0 -> magenta-pink #D77AB5 -> salmon/coral #F29C8C -> peach/orange #FFB46B near the horizon, with smooth gradient, faint horizontal banding, thin contrails and a few small birds.
- Foreground accents: hot pink #FF4FA3, magenta #C43AA0, teal/cyan #3FD0D0, warm yellow #FFD36B, sea-green #4FB89A, denim blue #5C7FC4, olive/forest green #3E6A3F.
- Background and silhouettes: lavender #9D84D6, mauve #B58BC9, pastel peach #FFD9A8, pale yellow #FFE9B0.
- The whole image must be saturated and luminous: bright sunset glow, not dark, not muddy, not monochrome purple. At least three clearly different hues must be visible (pink + orange/yellow + teal or blue accents).
- Daytime variant when the user's theme is a day scene: sky cyan #8ED8F0 to pale yellow at the horizon, turquoise water, pastel pink/lavender buildings, same flat graphic rendering and rim light.

BACKGROUND AND ENVIRONMENT
- Florida/Miami-style sub-tropical coastal setting treated as a flatter, lower-contrast, atmospheric backdrop: huge flat violet-purple palm tree silhouettes framing left and right, hazy pastel skyline of art-deco and modern towers, calm bay or beach with simple mirror-like reflections, bridges, gas stations with plain canopies, motels, parked classic muscle cars, trucks, pickup vehicles, palm-lined streets, small birds, a helicopter or plane.
- Everything behind the main subjects is simplified into big flat shapes, tinted by the sky colors and lighter than the foreground to create depth. The background is bright and open, never cluttered or dark.
- INTERIOR SCENES: keep the same look. Place big windows or open doors showing the sunset sky and palm silhouettes, let low golden sun rim-light the figures, use warm peach/coral walls with violet shadows and teal or pink accents. Do not make interiors dark purple or neon-lit; no nightclub gloom.

COMPOSITION
- Poster / key-art composition: one to three characters large in the foreground at three-quarter or torso-to-knee framing, slightly low camera angle, heroic and cool posture (leaning on a car, standing shoulder to shoulder, holding a pistol or bag, pulling a bandana over the face, walking toward the camera), looking at or past the camera with an intense stare.
- Strong figure/background separation by rim light and by detail contrast (sharp, detailed foreground; flat, hazy background).
- Fashion: realistic modern street and beach clothes (tank tops, cropped hoodies, graphic tees, open shirts, cut-off denim shorts, cargo pants, camo leggings, sneakers, hoop earrings, gold chains and bracelets, watches, bandanas, tattoos) in the palette above. Gritty yet glamorous, sun-drenched, rebellious mood.

TEXT AND BRANDING
- Do NOT write any text, words, letters, logos, neon signs, captions, titles, watermarks or game branding anywhere in the image unless the user explicitly asks for specific text. Signs, shirts, license plates and storefronts must be blank or purely graphic.
"""

